<style>
  .invalid-icon { font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block; opacity: 0.4; }
  .invalid-heading {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; color: #1A1410;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .invalid-sub {
    font-size: 15px; color: #8A7E6F; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .invalid-box {
    background: #F0EAE0; border-left: 3px solid #FAE8DE;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .invalid-box p { font-size: 14px; color: #6B5C4A; line-height: 1.55; }
  .divider { border: none; border-top: 1px solid #EBE4DB; margin: 24px 0; }
  .dashboard-link {
    display: block; text-align: center;
    font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #8A7E6F;
    text-decoration: none; padding: 10px;
    border: 1px solid #DDD5C8; border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .dashboard-link:hover { color: #1A1410; border-color: #B0A594; }
</style>

<span class="invalid-icon">⚠</span>

<h1 class="invalid-heading">Invalid approval link</h1>

<p class="invalid-sub">
  This link doesn't look right — it may have been truncated or modified by your email client.
</p>

<div class="invalid-box">
  <p>
    Please reopen the original ChurnGuard email and click the button directly.
    If the problem persists, the link may have already been used or may have expired.
  </p>
</div>

<hr class="divider">

<a href="<%= root_path %>" class="dashboard-link">
  View dashboard →
</a>
